 "sentences": [
  "There was a spring of light at the foot of a hill.",
  "Old Wen sat on a stone nearby.",
  "A clay jar glowed beside it.",
  "A smooth hollow lay open in the rock.",
  "A spiral shell lay on the slope.",
  "A boulder sat on the slope.",
  "Ada wanted to send a boat into the sky.",
  "She pushed the hollow hard, but it did not move.",
  "She moved the shell, and it settled into the hollow.",
  "She was delighted with the shell.",
  "She gave the boulder a hard push, and it split apart.",
  "A little carved boat lay among the pieces.",
  "A heap of pebbles lay on the ground.",
  "Ada wondered what the hollow needed.",
  "She felt sad about the boulder.",
  "She was delighted with the carved boat.",
  "\"What belongs in the hollow?\" Ada asked Wen.",
  "\"The carved boat belongs in the hollow,\" Wen said.",
  "Ada pushed the hollow hard.",
  "A shell-shaped cup took shape beside the hollow.",
  "\"What moves the carved boat?\" Ada asked Wen.",
  "\"I don't know what moves the carved boat,\" Wen said.",
  "Ada shook the jar, and it went dark.",
  "She was delighted with the jar.",
  "She wondered what the jar did.",
  "She shook the jar again, but it would not move.",
  "She felt anxious about the jar.",
  "She shoved the hollow, but it did not budge.",
  "She felt anxious about the cup.",
  "She felt sad about the jar.",
  "She moved the shell, and it came out of the hollow.",
  "She felt sad about the cup.",
  "She dipped the jar into the spring, and it began to glow.",
  "In time, she stopped thinking about the boulder.",
  "She touched the hollow, but nothing happened.",
  "She grew frustrated with the hollow.",
  "She pushed the hollow hard, but it did not move.",
  "She gave the hollow a hard push again, but it would not move.",
  "She shook the jar, and it went dark.",
  "She moved the shell, and it settled into the hollow.",
  "In time, she stopped thinking about the jar.",
  "She pressed on the hollow, but it did not budge.",
  "Again and again she tried the hollow and the jar, but nothing gave.",
  "She felt anxious about the jar again.",
  "She moved the carved boat, and it settled into the hollow.",
  "The shell came out of the hollow.",
  "Ada shoved the hollow, but nothing happened.",
  "She moved the carved boat, and it came out of the hollow.",
  "She pushed the hollow hard, but it did not move.",
  "She dipped the jar into the spring, and it began to glow.",
  "She was delighted with the jar.",
  "She moved the shell, and it settled into the hollow.",
  "She gave the hollow a hard push, but it would not move.",
  "She moved the carved boat, and it settled into the hollow.",
  "The shell came out of the hollow.",
  "Ada touched the hollow.",
  "A small skiff took shape beside the hollow.",
  "Ada realized that Wen had been right.",
  "\"What lifts the skiff?\" Ada asked Wen.",
  "\"I don't know what lifts the skiff,\" Wen said.",
  "Ada wondered what the skiff did.",
  "She shoved the skiff, and it rose into the air and came down on the far hill.",
  "The carved boat came out of the hollow.",
  "Ada laughed with joy."
